{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789224125,"nonce":"pWIO0aJdqCrjBOg0SRroWvUwriM=","message":"Scope is wider than short-circuits: any expression that creates control flow (a conditional expression, and/or, a match) and sits in an operand position fails the same way. The child finishes in a merge block and reports it through continuation_block, but Binary, Unary, Call, Field, Index and Cast never consult it, so the parent emits its own instruction into the block the child started in, before that block's branch, where the merge phi is not defined.\n\n    print(1 if side(1) else 2)         crash at the call\n    y = 1 + (3 if side(1) else 4)      crash at the add\n    print(side(1) or side(2))          crash at the call\n\nStatement-level lets and returns already consult continuation_block, which is why the same expressions work when bound to a name first.","files":null}]}